 6. 🛍️ Black Friday marathon 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The days of shoppers lining up outside of stores on Thanksgiving night and fighting over the season's hottest toys are giving way to a much calmer Black Friday shopping experience.

 A strategy that gained momentum during the pandemic to entice shoppers to spread out their spending has become a holiday retail staple, with businesses extending sales across weeks rather than a single day, Axios' Julianna Bragg reports. 👜 State of play: An estimated 182.7 million consumers are expected to shop during Thanksgiving weekend, down 2+% from last year, according to the National Retail Federation . 

 The dip is largely attributed to Americans shopping sooner, with 60% starting their holiday shopping by early November, the federation said. 📉 The share of shoppers planning to concentrate their purchases around Black Friday also fell from 25% to 17%, a Bank of America survey found. 

