 8. 🤖 1 for the road: AI plays Santa 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 This season is a first test of whether AI will become a holiday shopping force, Bloomberg's Spencer Soper reports . 

 McKinsey is bullish — projecting that agents capable of researching and buying merchandise will generate $1 trillion in economic activity in the U.S. by 2030. 👀 What's new: Google's "Universal Cart" lets users put items from multiple retailers in one cart and get alerted when prices drop.

 People shopping with Meta's Muse get 90 days of "price protection" if they find better deals after placing orders. Amazon is testing letting people text requests to Alexa. Friction point: London software firm Human Forward tested bots on 200 websites and found that half of the big retailers don't let AI assistants do the shopping.

